FkbOIA","review_id":"gXSIWy_CW7Dp2_w90gf21A","date":"2020-02-20T21:46:47","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9202535152435303,"text_excerpt":"I have experienced Lucky's a few times in the past. Although I do love a good divey feeling bar, I have really only frequented here because of the location. I am not even sure if the name has remained the same for this place. But for the Mardi Gras I have been to over the last decade, this has been a great place to buy a drink and use the restroom. This past time, it was the weekend before Mardi Gras weekend. So the crowds aren't as bad and I'm sure the bathroom rules are less strict. But as I remember, they were not nearly as strict as many of the other businesses around on the actual weekend. For the most part, the bartenders are pretty attentive and friendly. There was once this past t..."},{"business_id":"ufjjhbpzlG91sQCFFkbOIA","review_id":"_GGCoydqdN86mtmgMHmaSQ","date":"2005-07-10T17:33:59","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.919884443283081,"text_excerpt":"Lucky's is a nice place on St. Charles with a nice bar and friendly staff. The bar food is prettty decent too, though nothing special. Good place to watch sports on TV."},{"business_id":"ufjjhbpzlG91sQCFFkbOIA","review_id":"4KqxMCw4usXqBIahF8VOfA","date":"2009-03-01T05:00:45","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9172816276550293,"text_excerpt":"Lucky's is a great neighborhood bar. The staff is tolerant of your nonsense, but not to the point where you're allowed to abuse other patrons. I like that in a bar."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
